# Write change notes

Once people rely on a Civica page, a dashboard’s help text or an automation’s description, some changes to it need a change note.

Skip the note if you only:

- corrected a typing mistake
- changed the style, such as a heading’s wording or a view’s layout
- fixed or removed a broken link, unless people need what it leads to

Add a note if you have:

- added information that means people must act differently or now know something new
- taken out guidance that was out of date or could mislead
- changed a requirement, such as the lowest Home Assistant version Civica supports
- changed the Civica licence or privacy notice

<h2 id="know-who-can-see-change-notes">Know who can see change notes</h2>

Anyone can read a change note. Notes for a Civica page appear under “See all updates” on that page, newest first, with the date. In a dashboard or an automation, anyone who can open it can read the note.

So every note must:

- say plainly what changed, and where on the page, view or card
- be kept for changes that matter, so people do not read about ones that do not affect them

Notes are public, so leave out names, addresses and anything private.

Open “See all updates” on any Civica page to see how notes look.

<h2 id="wg-091">Write clear change notes</h2>

You are ready to write when you:

- know what changed and why it matters to the people who use it
- have asked anyone you need to help you explain the change and its effects

Where you can, put the new information in the note, so people learn it without opening the page.

For a large change, sum up:

- what changed
- where, such as the section, view, card or step number

Make each note:

- precise
- written in full sentences
- led by the change that matters most

A note that only says something was updated tells people nothing. Name the change.

Good change notes:

- The Civica palettes are now 7 theme colours. If you used a palette such as Civica Civic Cobalt Vivid, choose a theme colour again in your profile.
- Removed the restart from Install Civica. After you add the theme files, reloading themes is enough.
- The button on the Living room heating card now reads “Boost for 1 hour”, not “Boost”.
- The landing light now stays on for 5 minutes after the last movement, not 2 minutes.

Poor change notes:

- Help updated.
- Changed the files behind this page so its summary shows in search.
- Added preview images for sharing this page.
- Removed broken link.
